Subject: [PATCH 191/206] Correct three errors in the message of f24498a3740
 (no code change)

The ref-transaction hook refuses a non-fast-forward update of this
branch, so f24498a3740's message cannot be amended; this empty commit
carries the correction instead. The code in f24498a3740 is unchanged
and is what was verified.

1. "Keeping the narrower upstream condition means the CPU branch stays
   reachable for a thread that is genuinely not simulating." -- wrong,
   and backwards. Upstream, and the state restored by f24498a3740, is
   the WIDER condition "if (FLAG_use_simulator)". f5b94e5b439 was the
   one that narrowed it to
   "FLAG_use_simulator && thread->is_simulating() != 0". Restoring the
   wider condition makes the CPU branch LESS reachable in simulator
   mode, not more. That sentence should be struck; it is not an
   argument for the revert and nothing was measured to support it.

2. "the added disjunct" -- it is a conjunct, and it was added by
   f5b94e5b439, not by f24498a3740.

3. "the simulator branch at exceptions.cc:630 ... the CPU branch at
   :646" -- the line numbers are 631 (Simulator::Current()->JumpToFrame)
   and 676 (StubCode::JumpToFrame). :646 is HWASAN/ASAN bookkeeping, not
   a branch. The counts themselves, 102 and 0 on p4 in simulator mode,
   were re-measured on the build of f24498a3740 with
   "lldb -b" and "br set -f exceptions.cc -l 631 -G true" /
   "-l 676 -G true", and are correct.

What stands unchanged: both reverted hunks are not load-bearing. On the
build of f24498a3740, xcodebuild/ProductSimARM64_cpu with 0 pending
ninja steps, hi + p1..p8 give 9 PASS 0 FAIL under --no-use_simulator
and 9 PASS 0 FAIL in default simulator mode.

